Author-Name: Saira Ishfaq Ishfaq
Author-Name: Imran Khan
Author-Name: Tazeem Shah
Author-Name: Raja Jamil
Title: The Role of Microfinance in Poverty Reduction: Evidence from South Asia
Abstract: This study analyzed the impact of micro finance and macroeconomic variables on poverty at three levels. The paper covers the time period of 08 years from 2005 to 2012. A panel of 06 selected SAARC countries was taken including India, Nepal, Pakistan, Sri Lanka, Bangladesh and Bhutan. Panel data regression model was used in the study. A key finding is that microfinance reduces extreme poverty and literacy also plays a major in poverty reduction. Other findings and recommendations are discussed in the paper.
Keywords: Microfinance,Poverty,Regression Model,Hausamn Test,South Asia
